          "text": "Stamp and carving",
          "centered": true,
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "type": "modopedia:text",
          "x": 2,
          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "A stamp first stores a pattern in its local editor, then writes it back as a PaintPattern. Shift+right-click opens the editor; left applies, right erases, R rotates, and X+drag"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "resizes."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• StampCanvasMaterial decides the carved color and effect value.\n• The stamp revision prevents an old snapshot from overwriting a newer pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• A stamp copies structure; it does not automatically solve recognition or spatial relations."
    },
